---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'August 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How USAPrizes.com researches, rates, and updates its sweepstakes casino reviews and lottery content, and how affiliate relationships work."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' }]} />
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>How we review</h2>
      <p>
        Every sweepstakes casino review on this site is based on hands-on account creation,
        redemption testing, and monitoring of published terms. We evaluate each operator on:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Redemption speed and reliability</li>
        <li>Payment and redemption methods offered</li>
        <li>Game selection and software providers</li>
        <li>State availability and current legal status</li>
        <li>Bonus terms and how clearly they're disclosed</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Ratings and rankings reflect our own editorial judgment. They are not paid placements
        &mdash; no operator can buy a higher rating or a spot on our
        <a href="/casinos/best-sweepstakes-casinos/">best sweepstakes casinos</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to sweepstakes casino operators on this site are affiliate links. If you sign
        up through one of those links, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
        This is disclosed on every page where it applies. Affiliate relationships never
        determine whether an operator is reviewed, how it's rated, or whether it appears in our
        rankings.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
      <p>
        Sweepstakes-casino legality and promotional terms change frequently. We show a visible
        "last updated" date on every review and legality page, and we re-check our top-ranked
        operators on a monthly cadence at minimum. Lottery results are pulled from public state
        data feeds shortly after each drawing; if a discrepancy ever appears, the official state
        lottery result always governs.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot an error, contact us via the details on our <a href="/about/">About</a>
        page and we will investigate and correct it promptly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
